# CMS22 Blood Pressure Control Cognitive Support Example
library "CMS22 BP Control Cognitive Support Example".

/*
Clinical Reasoning Language (CRL) — v2.1.0 grammar reference example.

A second canonical small example built on the **CMS22 (Controlling High
Blood Pressure)** quality measure, framed as a point-of-care cognitive
support workflow for hypertension management. Sister to
clinical-reasoning-language-example.crl (which targets CMS69 BMI
screening); pick whichever fits your scenario.

The full quality-measure encoding lives in
features/cql-pattern-mining/results/models/cms22-split/. This file shows
the cognitive-support facet: at an encounter, what should the clinician
do so the patient ends up in CMS22's numerator (BP controlled or a
documented appropriate follow-up plan)?

Same grammar conventions as the CMS69 example — see that file for the
surface rules. This file's structural variety:
  - `defined as ( ... sem-or ... )`: multi-source composition
    (BP reading from a panel OR standalone systolic/diastolic obs).
  - `defined as ( "X" sem-and sem-not "Y" )`: the sem-not example
    (last reading is hypertensive but NOT yet diagnosed).
  - `definition is X high`, `definition is X performed`,
    `definition is X documented`: narrative-predicate body kinds.
  - `any:` / `all:` recommendation blocks inside `when/then` bodies.
  - `use decision` chaining between top-level + sub-decisions.
  - `recommend activity` with `do not perform`.
*/

// ============ Decisions ============

// Top-level cognitive-support decision for hypertension. Walked at
// every qualifying encounter for an adult patient. The when/then
// branches mirror CMS22's clinical flow:
//   1. capture a BP reading if none for this visit,
//   2. if BP is hypertensive, drive treatment OR documentation,
//   3. if BP is normal but the patient has hypertension on file,
//      remind the clinician to confirm continued control.
decision "CMS22 BP Control Strategy":

- when "Patient Eligible For BP Cognitive Support" then:
  - when "No BP Reading At This Encounter" then recommend activity "Measure BP".
  - when "Has Hypertensive Reading" then use decision "Recommend Hypertension Intervention".
  - when "Has Normal Reading With Hypertension On File" then recommend activity "Confirm Continued Control".
- end when

// Hypertensive-reading sub-decision. CMS22 accepts any one of:
// a medication order, a follow-up rescreen order, or a documented
// lifestyle/dietary referral. `any:` says any one of these
// recommendations satisfies the measure.
decision "Recommend Hypertension Intervention":

- when "Has Confirmed Hypertension Diagnosis" then:
  any:
  - recommend activity "Order Antihypertensive Medication".
  - recommend activity "Order Follow-up Rescreen".
  - recommend activity "Order Lifestyle Referral".
- end when
- when "Hypertensive Reading Without Diagnosis" then:
  all:
  - recommend activity "Order Follow-up Rescreen".
  - recommend activity "Document Provisional Hypertension".
- end when
- when "Has Antihypertensive Contraindication" then recommend activity "Contraindicated Antihypertensive".


// ============ Activities ============

activity "Measure BP":
- request CPGCollectInformation.
- with "Blood Pressure Panels VS".

activity "Order Antihypertensive Medication":
- request CPGMedicationRequest.
- with "Antihypertensive Medications VS".
- because `Patient has confirmed hypertension and an in-range encounter`.

activity "Order Follow-up Rescreen":
- request CPGServiceRequest.
- with "Follow Up Within 4 Weeks VS".

activity "Order Lifestyle Referral":
- request CPGServiceRequest.
- with "Lifestyle Recommendation VS".
- because `Lifestyle counselling is the first-line intervention for stage-1 hypertension`.

activity "Confirm Continued Control":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `Confirm BP control remains adequate; no escalation needed this visit`.

activity "Document Provisional Hypertension":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `Single hypertensive reading without prior diagnosis — document provisional status and rescreen`.
- because `Quality measure requires confirmation across encounters before a hypertension diagnosis is durable`.

activity "Contraindicated Antihypertensive":
- request do not perform CPGMedicationRequest.
- with "Antihypertensive Medications VS".
- because `Patient has a documented contraindication to antihypertensive pharmacotherapy`.


// ============ Terminologies ============

terminology "Blood Pressure Panels VS":
- valueset is `http://loinc.org/vs/85354-9`.

terminology "Standalone Systolic BP VS":
- valueset is `http://loinc.org/vs/8480-6`.

terminology "Standalone Diastolic BP VS":
- valueset is `http://loinc.org/vs/8462-4`.

terminology "Hypertension Diagnoses VS":
- valueset is `http://cts.nlm.nih.gov/fhir/ValueSet/2.16.840.1.113883.3.600.263`.

terminology "Antihypertensive Medications VS":
- valueset is `http://cts.nlm.nih.gov/fhir/ValueSet/2.16.840.1.113883.3.526.1577`.

terminology "Follow Up Within 4 Weeks VS":
- valueset is `http://cts.nlm.nih.gov/fhir/ValueSet/2.16.840.1.113883.3.526.3.1578`.

terminology "Lifestyle Recommendation VS":
- valueset is `http://cts.nlm.nih.gov/fhir/ValueSet/2.16.840.1.113883.3.526.3.1581`.

terminology "Antihypertensive Contraindication VS":
- valueset is `urn:example:placeholder`.

terminology "Medical Reason VS":
- valueset is `http://cts.nlm.nih.gov/fhir/ValueSet/2.16.840.1.113883.3.526.3.1007`.

terminology "Patient Declined VS":
- valueset is `http://cts.nlm.nih.gov/fhir/ValueSet/2.16.840.1.113883.3.526.3.1582`.


// ============ Concepts ============

// --- Asserted concepts (coded from a terminology) ---

concept "Blood Pressure Panels":
- type is Observation.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- value type is Quantity.
- coded from "Blood Pressure Panels VS".

concept "Standalone Systolic BP Observations":
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- coded from "Standalone Systolic BP VS".

concept "Standalone Diastolic BP Observations":
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- coded from "Standalone Diastolic BP VS".

concept "Hypertension Diagnoses":
- type is Condition.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- coded from "Hypertension Diagnoses VS".

concept "Antihypertensive Medications":
- type is MedicationRequest.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- coded from "Antihypertensive Medications VS".

concept "Follow-up Within 4 Weeks":
- type is ServiceRequest.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- coded from "Follow Up Within 4 Weeks VS".

concept "Lifestyle Recommendations":
- type is ServiceRequest.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- coded from "Lifestyle Recommendation VS".

concept "Antihypertensive Contraindication":
- type is Observation.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- coded from "Antihypertensive Contraindication VS".

concept "Medical Reasons":
- type is Observation.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- coded from "Medical Reason VS".

concept "Patient Declined Reasons":
- type is Observation.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- coded from "Patient Declined VS".


// --- Composition concepts: multi-source BP reading ---

// A BP reading can come from a paired panel observation OR from a
// pair of standalone systolic + diastolic observations. The cognitive
// support layer doesn't care which source — it just needs a reading.
concept "BP Reading":
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- defined as
(
   "Blood Pressure Panels"
   sem-or
   "Standalone Systolic BP Observations"
   sem-or
   "Standalone Diastolic BP Observations"
).


// --- Predicate-kind concepts: narrative body + composing concept pair ---

concept "Last BP Reading At This Encounter Selection":
- meta is `Picks the latest BP observation tied to the current encounter`.
- evidence is `Calculated by Smile`.
- definition is most recent "BP Reading".

concept "Last BP Reading At This Encounter":
- type is Observation.
- value type is Quantity.
- defined as "Last BP Reading At This Encounter Selection".


// --- sem-not example: hypertensive reading without confirmed diagnosis ---

// The patient's last reading is hypertensive, but no Hypertension
// Diagnoses are on file — a single high reading is not yet a durable
// diagnosis under CMS22. The cognitive support layer flags this so
// the clinician confirms across encounters before committing.
concept "Hypertensive Reading Without Diagnosis":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- defined as
(
   "Has Hypertensive Reading"
   sem-and
   sem-not "Hypertension Diagnoses"
).


// --- Cognitive-support predicates (narrative bodies feeding the decision) ---

concept "Patient Eligible For BP Cognitive Support":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- defined as
(
   sem-not "Medical Reasons"
   sem-and
   sem-not "Patient Declined Reasons"
).

concept "No BP Reading At This Encounter":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- definition is without documented "BP Reading".

concept "Has Hypertensive Reading":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- definition is "Last BP Reading At This Encounter" high.

concept "Has Normal Reading With Hypertension On File":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- defined as
(
   "Has Normal Reading"
   sem-and
   "Has Confirmed Hypertension Diagnosis"
).

concept "Has Normal Reading":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- definition is "Last BP Reading At This Encounter" normal.

concept "Has Confirmed Hypertension Diagnosis":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- definition is "Hypertension Diagnoses" active.

concept "Has Antihypertensive Contraindication":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- definition is documented "Antihypertensive Contraindication".


